#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:1
#: db3f4f8362664dd38c1eb4474c609cf3
msgid "Bit-exactness & parity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:3
#: 445f3f53722e40adab0b637ff2e42064
msgid "parsecore's star ratings and pp values are **bit-for-bit identical** to the official osu! implementation. This is the project's core promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:6
#: 6d264449a5434a0bb5343baf0c5aed8f
msgid "How it's achieved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:8
#: 4902d43ccf314b2696e831edcf7a83c9
msgid "Reproducing the reference *closely* is not enough parsecore reproduces it *exactly*, including the floating-point behaviour of the original:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:12
#: 9249098924704895b174690532c459ae
msgid "**f32 intermediates** positions, curve math and several constants are computed in 32-bit floats, matching the game client (and rosu-pp's Rust ``f32``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:14
#: bac6bdd06cda45be8ff2ebbe1cbcb30d
msgid "**Explicit integer powers** ``x * x * x`` where the reference uses ``DiffUtils.Pow(x, 3)``, not ``math.pow`` (they can differ in the last bit)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:16
#: fd849db0f71f43eaabd572a336d08f52
msgid "**IEEE semantics** division by zero, NaN handling and negative-base powers follow Rust/C# rules via dedicated helpers (``ieee_div``, ``rust_min``, ...), never Python's exceptions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:19
#: b535689401eb4d3ba97b26582342819b
msgid "**Exact RNG and sorting** the legacy converters use osu!stable's RNG in the exact call order, and the C# unstable sort is reproduced for nested slider objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:23
#: 98c332bc4aae4a1ca23b605bee3b6a76
msgid "How it's verified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:25
#: 225c00aec2374b9e9d636e64df4630fc
msgid "Correctness is enforced by a parity test suite that compares parsecore against an oracle built from the official `ppy.osu.Game` packages (with rosu-pp as a secondary cross-check):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:29
#: 9023d595af6a405b87c0c6be3f0d01e0
msgid "4,400+ cases: star ratings and pp across all four rulesets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:30
#: a4958aaecf334dabb215e65ae74f3712
msgid "extended mod matrix (EZ/HR/DT/NC/HT/HD/FL/TD/RX/AP/SO, key mods 1K-9K, combinations)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:31
#: 62c14847267b4768a97cdf250c7e4b5d
msgid "all convert directions, native maps, edge-case and pathological maps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:32
#: a505ee957a1e474faac3792a25455b56
msgid "randomized full score states, partial states, fails, lazer & stable scores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:33
#: 0c169f7bdd9b4c55b3bc121274a3b8dd
msgid "**result: 0 differences every value bit-identical to the official implementation**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/bit-exactness.md:37
#: 782081075cc44fff95791953dd6fd097
msgid "After a pp rework deploys, public calculators and bots that rely on outdated libraries can disagree with parsecore. When in doubt: new scores set in-game receive exactly the values parsecore computes."
msgstr ""

